 "notes": "Source: ICC free viewer (codes.iccsafe.org), rendered headlessly 2026-10-27: IRC2021P2 ch5/ch8/ch11, IRC2024V2.1 ch5/ch8/ch11, IECC2021P1 + IECC2021P2 ch4, IECC2024P1 ch4. Values were parsed from the page text, not typed in by hand; the IRC 2021 DFL #2 floor_40psf and ceiling rows also match the City of Sacramento handout CDD-0277. | Table numbers: ceiling joists = Table R802.5.1(1) and rafters = Table R802.4.1(1) in both 2021 and 2024. The brief had these two numbers swapped. | 2024 renumbering: none of the tables used here changed number. R502.3.1(1), R502.3.1(2), R802.4.1(1), R802.5.1(1), R402.1.3 and N1102.1.3 are the same in 2021 and 2024. | Rafters: a roof live load 20 psf table exists (R802.4.1(1), ceiling not attached, L/180), so it is used here, not the 30 psf ground snow table. The snow tables are R802.4.1(3) to (8) for 30/50/70 psf ground snow. Spans are horizontal projection. Footnote a of R802.4.1(1): if ceiling joists or rafter ties sit higher in the attic, apply the factor in Table R802.4.1(9). | Ceiling joist table has only one dead load column, 5 psf (not 10 psf), and covers 2x4 to 2x10. | '>26-0' stands for the table footnote 'span exceeds 26 feet' (Note a in R802.5.1(1), Note b in R802.4.1(1)). | Every span cell for the four #2 species is identical in IRC 2021 and IRC 2024 (compared cell by cell). In these tables spruce-pine-fir #2 equals spruce-pine-fir #1. | IECC 2021 printings differ on wood frame walls. First printing (IECC2021P1): CZ 4 and CZ 5/Marine 4 '20+5 or 13+10ci or 0+15', CZ 6-8 '20+5ci or 13+10ci or 0+20'. Second printing (IECC2021P2) and IRC 2021 P2: CZ 4-8 '30 or 20&5ci or 13&10ci or 0&20ci', CZ 3 '20 or 13&5ci or 0&15ci'. The values above use the second printing. | Notation: '&' is kept as the current ICC text writes it (first value cavity, second value continuous). IECC2021P1 writes '+'. The 2024 floor row writes '+'. | Footnote letters were removed from cells. 2021 fenestration_u carries footnote i: max 0.32 in CZ 3-8 above 4,000 ft elevation or in windborne debris regions. 2024 fenestration_u CZ 5-8 carries footnote g: max 0.30 in Marine 4 and CZ 5-8 under the same two conditions. Basement and crawl wall CZ 3 '5ci or 13' carry a footnote: not required in Warm Humid locations. In 2021 the wood wall cells for CZ 3-8 carry an h mark. | Source typos: IECC2021P1 shows CZ 3 and 4 fenestration as '.30' (= 0.30). IRC 2021 shows crawl wall CZ 7-8 as '1 9' (= 19). | 2021 slab_r: heated slabs also need R-5 under the full slab area (footnote d). 2024 splits the slab into unheated (slab_r) and heated (heated_slab_r) rows. It also adds skylight SHGC and insulation-entirely-above-roof-deck rows, and its 'shgc' is vertical fenestration only. | IECC 2024 R402.1.3 and IRC 2024 N1102.1.3 have the same values, and so do IECC 2021 (P2) and IRC 2021 N1102.1.3. From 2021 to 2024: ceiling R drops (CZ 2-3 49 to 38, CZ 4-8 60 to 49) and skylight U drops; fenestration U is added in CZ 0-1 (NR to 0.50) and tightened in CZ 5-8. Local adoptions often amend this table."
